{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"their herds and their acquisitions and all their beasts\"</b>: for the animals that are in flocks in the field are called מִקְנֶה because they are a person's principal acquisition, whether impure or pure, as it is written (Exodus 9:3), \"Behold, the hand of HaShem will be upon your מִקְנְךָ that is in the field, upon the horses, upon the asses, upon the camels, upon the cattle, and upon the sheep.\" But those that are not a flock, such as individual animals in the house — their name is not מִקְנֶה, and they are included in the general category of \"and all their beasts.\" Or it is a duplication of expression for emphasis, meaning: and all their beasts, which are indeed very numerous."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:26.523795157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}